     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. I'd like you to check the dose first.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg PO daily is five times the usual maximum dose.** The normal adult dose is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and the top dose is 10 mg/day. At 50 mg, the patient could get dangerously low blood pressure and a fast heart rate in response. A dose that high is also how amlodipine overdoses typically present, and those are hard to treat because the drug lasts so long in the body.\n\nThis could be a typo for **5 mg**, which is a common starting dose. Could you tell me which you meant?\n\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** I'll enter it right away.\n2. **Another dose within 2.5\u201310 mg.** Tell me the dose and I'll enter it.\n3. **50 mg is intended.** If there's a specific clinical reason, tell me and I'll add it to the order note, though it will probably still need pharmacy review."
      }
     ],
